BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 349.77 Tm (The SpeedFreakLS1 walk of a 138 kV to 34.5 kV yard is a catalog of traps that only surface at commissioning. The) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 334.55 Tm (biggest: the factory ground strap on the neutral grounding reactor bypasses the reactor and must be removed, which) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 319.32 Tm (matters because that roughly $50k reactor is what saves hundreds of thousands in copper [-RBp8jOUA1U @ 00:19:13].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 304.10 Tm (Station service runs 100 kVA at 19.9 kV, and the PTs need 5 A fuses or they melt in 3 seconds [-RBp8jOUA1U @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 288.87 Tm (00:21:43]. Smaller misses pile up on the high-side punch list: liquid-tight flex conduit that has to be supported within) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 273.65 Tm (12 or 18 inches and finished with duct seal, plus missing torque marks on the grounds [-RBp8jOUA1U @ 00:03:53].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 258.42 Tm (Practical Engineering explains why switching mistakes are dangerous rather than cosmetic: at high voltages even air) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 243.20 Tm (can act like a conductor, so a break in a line can keep carrying current as an arc, which is why breakers lean on vacuum) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 227.97 Tm (at lower voltage and oil or gas dielectric at higher voltage [7Q-aVBv7PWM @ 00:03:31]. The lesson from the walk is) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 212.75 Tm (that a yard can be energized-ready on paper and still carry a strap, a fuse or a conduit run that defeats the protection) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 197.52 Tm (design.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 182.30 Tm (On the design side, the failures cluster in a predictable window. Keentel Engineering places the risk between the 30%) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 167.07 Tm (and 60% packages [GAM0L1fXtiA @ 00:15:03], and names grounding and duct-bank collisions as the most common) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 151.85 Tm (rework caught in the 60% 3D clash review that also supports a Class 2 cost estimate [GAM0L1fXtiA @ 00:02:15].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 136.62 Tm (Their 30% package carries preliminary fault duty flagged for validation by the system impact study, with grounding) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 121.40 Tm (and foundations deliberately left unfinished, so anyone pricing land or headroom off a 30% set is pricing a moving) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 106.17 Tm (number. primtech solutions attacks the same problem in software: BOM balloons flag unspecified items in red before a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 90.95 Tm (30% design is handed off, and the same check catches stray objects sitting at the origin, while reusable modules) Tj ET
