BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 637.77 Tm (The most expensive mistake practitioners report is running the asset into the ground. Zami of Clearspot uses a car) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 622.55 Tm (redline analogy: warranties often assume 365 cycles a year, LFP should stay within 5-95%, and running 200 cycles) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 607.32 Tm (instead of 100 could cut life from 20 to 16 years [tFP2z1s7IrM @ 00:34:55]. Zami also names the incentive problem:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 592.10 Tm (traders on quarterly bonuses chase revenue, and gaining 5% revenue at the cost of 20% of asset life is a bad trade) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 576.87 Tm ([tFP2z1s7IrM @ 00:36:10]. Academie ?nergie puts a number on ignoring wear: accounting for degradation cuts over) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 561.65 Tm (22% of annual net profit at 1 MWh and over 12% at 2 MWh, and the two mistakes flagged are ignoring degradation) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 546.42 Tm (and oversizing [V57-D23t6Lo @ 00:03:44]. Jerzy Kuzminski adds the contract sting: daily cycle caps can void) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 531.20 Tm (warranties, so aggressive dispatch can cost the owner warranty cover outright [fDBjJyTGWDQ @ 00:18:25]. Zami's) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 515.97 Tm (charging advice points the same way, since fast charging leaves cells unbalanced and spreading a 4-hour battery's) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 500.75 Tm (charge over 5-6 hours is better. The economics check is simple: every extra cycle has to earn more than the life it burns,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 485.52 Tm (and the trader dispatching it rarely carries that cost.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 470.30 Tm (Contract and supplier traps come next. Jerzy Kuzminski reports a supplier that shipped a container plus cells only,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 455.07 Tm (notes that warranties are multiplicative so three stacked 98% guarantees land at about 94%, and warns that EMS fees) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 439.85 Tm (can take 20-30% of arbitrage revenue while SCADA can cost as much as the container [fDBjJyTGWDQ @ 00:22:19].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 424.62 Tm (Kuzminski's rule is that technical specifications must be an annex to the contract, not a separate marketing document,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 409.40 Tm (because a quoted 92% round-trip efficiency becomes 85-87% after three years [fDBjJyTGWDQ @ 00:23:17]. STG) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 394.17 Tm (Nations Energy points out that neither the supplier nor the EPC checks degradation, thermal runaway and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 378.95 Tm (grid-connection risk end to end, which is the gap it pitches an independent engineer with zero supplier commissions to) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 363.72 Tm (fill [AVf_DgVRB3w @ 00:05:25]. Andy Willis of Kona Energy says developers leave insurance too late; insurers) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 348.50 Tm (belong in the room before design and supplier choice, so battery and transformer suppliers get vetted for bankability) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 333.27 Tm ([UI-9nmVEA9U @ 00:08:38]. Kuzminski also flags the integrator spread: 20-30 cell makers but hundreds of) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 318.05 Tm (integrators, often using the same cells and quoting X versus X plus 20%. Every one of these costs lands on the owner) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 302.82 Tm (after signature, which is why the paperwork gets fought before it does.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 287.60 Tm (The project-killers often sit outside the battery itself. Ravi Sharma of Deriva warns that network-upgrade allocations of) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 272.37 Tm (tens to hundreds of millions of dollars can kill a project [LhT4VVDW7CI @ 00:14:10]. BESS Engineer lists the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 257.15 Tm (cancellation triggers: no fire-safety approval, a grid connection that is too expensive, or no long-term service plan) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 241.92 Tm ([r852ohYdDhc @ 00:01:48]. Logistics is the next squeeze. Marcus at Fluence says denser, heavier units no longer fit a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 226.70 Tm (high cube container and now need break-bulk and flatbed trailers instead of curtain-siders, ocean carriers resist the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 211.47 Tm (cargo, Fluence competes with the wind industry for deck space, vessel schedules are unreliable, and the coming) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 196.25 Tm (bottleneck is ADR-licensed drivers and low-bed trailers [fzdDu4tWnGQ @ 00:06:58]. Field's Emma shows how design) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 181.02 Tm (drifts under a live consent: a project started at 200 MW in September 2023, was 300 MW in the same footprint six) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 165.80 Tm (months later, and got a new layout in December 2024, so Emma recommends a Rochdale envelope approach and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 150.57 Tm (expects non-material amendments or s73 applications for changes as small as 20 cm of height or ?20 units) Tj ET
